        "original_id": "d0d92983-9c69-5074-9fad-17d37cdce0b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Northern Rhodesia, Southern Rhodesia, Zambia, Zimbabwe, Zambezi\n- Organizations: British South Africa Company, British government\n- Concepts: protectorates, colonial administration\n\nFacts:\n- The British South Africa Company officially designated the territory north of the Zambezi as Northern Rhodesia.\n- The British South Africa Company dubbed the territory south of the Zambezi as Southern Rhodesia.\n- From 1924, the British government administered Northern Rhodesia as a protectorate under conditions similar to other British-administered protectorates.\n- In 1924, the special provisions that had been required when Northern Rhodesia was administered by the British South Africa Company were terminated.\n- Northern Rhodesia has been Zambia since 1964.\n- Southern Rhodesia became Zimbabwe in 1980.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "93abffdc-c2b2-537f-819b-e063f2d268e9",
        "text": "Page: Rhodesia (region). Sentence: The territory to the north of the Zambezi was officially designated Northern Rhodesia by the Company, and has been Zambia since 1964; that to the south, which the Company dubbed Southern Rhodesia, became Zimbabwe in 1980.\nPage: Northern Rhodesia. Sentence: From 1924 it was administered by the British government as a protectorate under similar conditions to other British-administered protectorates, and the special provisions required when it was administered by BSAC were terminated.",
